WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.730
Let me explain the situation.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.400
Urachi is trying to erase all abilities from Sakurada,

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.900
while I'm planning to protect them.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.610
In other words,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.490
our opinions are polar opposites.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:18.950
That's why I summoned Urachi
to talk things through.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:23.000
But I had no intention of listening to Asai.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.380
I just played along,

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.590
planning to capture him.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.880
And that's how I decided to kidnap Urachi.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:31.630
Wait a second.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.550
I'm so lost.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.720
How does talking lead into kidnapping?

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.220
I wouldn't be able to negotiate with him
if we stuck to proper methods.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.230
That's why I had to make sure
Urachi wouldn't disappear on me

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.440
and bind him to a chair, forcefully if necessary.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.980
Kei, I'm on Director's side.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.940
That's another reason I wanted you to drive.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.030
What?

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:57.120
You were on Urachi's side before the reset as well.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.160
You believed abilities shouldn't exist.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.660
So if I have to convince you both anyway,

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.870
it's more efficient to convince you together.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.130
Your logic is crazy.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:10.210
If Director tells me to stop the car, I will.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.630
I have no choice then.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.880
Let's take a classic hostage.

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.970
Kei, you're going too far.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:22.100
You're right, I really don't want to do this.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.680
It's unfortunately a necessity, though.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.600
There's no way it's necessary.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:26.560
Director.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.270
What is it?

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.400
It's just as you're saying.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.280
It seems I've become Asai Kei's accomplice.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.530
You're siding with him?

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.660
For now. Seems like I have no other choice.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:43.910
So basically, you're prioritizing your job
as a teacher over your job with the Bureau?

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.500
This has nothing to do with me being a teacher.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.920
I don't get it.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.750
Even if he can't stab you,

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.960
he sure can stab himself.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.220
If I stopped the car,

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.430
he'd become a hostage himself.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:02.720
Of course I'd rather avoid such measures.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.640
He really hates violence, you see.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.350
I'm sure of it.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.730
Doing things you hate is difficult.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.610
And adults are responsible
for looking after children.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:17.780
If either of us has to make a difficult choice,

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.110
the adult should go first.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.410
Let's begin, then.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.510
The door has disappeared.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.510
We've been trapped here.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:11.230
I've made a hole in the gas tank of the Bureau's car.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.770
Can I ask you to take care of that next?

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.230
Unlock those two bikes.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.320
Are we stealing them?

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.360
We should be getting out of here soon.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.280
Aren't you trying to save the world?

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.280
Those bikes are in a no-bike-parking zone,
so no one can complain if we take them.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.280
I'm not trying to be good,
I'm trying to save the world.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.740
I don't see the difference.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.410
If someone hits you,
being good means not resisting,

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.170
while punching them back is
a step towards saving the world.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.380
Isn't that a pretty subjective definition of "saving"?

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:42.510
Those who wish to save the world know
what's right for the world to be saved.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.350
The Bureau members used some kind of ability.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:47.970
Let's hurry.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:48.890
No choice now.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.020
There they are!

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.520
<i>Around twenty seconds until my ability activates...</i>

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.150
<i>Will I not make it?</i>

00:04:58.520 --> 00:04:59.980
Look into their eyes.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:05.570
<i>Five...</i>

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.570
<i>Four... Three...</i>

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.080
<i>Two... One...</i>

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:10.700
<i>Zero!</i>

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.130
Stop that!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.210
Be quiet!

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.300
What?

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.970
Nice, Sakagami, Oka Eri.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:29.140
I'd rather use my ability myself, though.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.430
Too bad no one ever looks me in the eyes.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.390
Well, can't blame them.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.520
There we go.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.520
Everyone ready?

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:38.770
Let's go!

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.950
You're sounding awfully cute.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.580
Warn us next time you want
to do something this crazy!

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.500
What are you here for?

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.170
To meet someone.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.260
Not you, though.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.670
You're not running away?

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.760
It's not my job to run away.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.890
Job?

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:12.600
You mean what Asai Kei instructed you to do?

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.020
Yes, that's right.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:17.180
You put too much faith in him.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.690
He got rid of you.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.480
I don't understand.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.110
If you're the only one he left behind here,

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.610
isn't that the logical explanation?

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:28.650
I'm sure he knew you'd
be captured by the Bureau here.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.490
There's nothing wrong with me getting captured.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.580
Also, I won't get captured.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:37.580
Even alone, I'm capable of capturing you.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:41.130
But it's not just the two of us here.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:46.170
You probably can't take on two ability users.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.170
That's true.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:52.220
Seems like you're the one who
has to deal with two, though?

00:06:55.720 --> 00:07:00.310
I see not everything always
goes as Asai Kei planned.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:08.990
Do you really think you can convince me?

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.450
Yes, of course.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:14.870
If I explain what you gain from my plan,
you'll agree with me for sure.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.450
Well, whatever.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.910
I'm a victim of a kidnapping.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.460
Can't wait to hear what you have to say.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.090
Have you ever heard of the plank of Carneades?

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:26.630
Yeah.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:32.130
It's a skeptical thought experiment
about making life-or-death choices.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.260
When a ship is wrecked,

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.310
everyone aboard gets thrown into the sea.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:42.940
One man somehow succeeds in grabbing
onto a plank floating on the surface.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:47.020
But the plank can support only one person.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:51.280
And then another reaches for the plank.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:55.410
If he grabs onto it as well, both with drown.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.540
That's why he pushes the other man off.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.870
And so one man drowns, while the other is saved.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:03.710
Do you think that's the right decision?

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.920
In my opinion, yes.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:09.710
One of them surviving is better than both drowning.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:15.260
I also believe that humans should always
give their very best to survive.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.470
I see.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.970
What about you?

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:22.140
Please don't tell me you'd find
a way for both of them to survive.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.730
That's exactly what I think.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:27.150
Both of them surviving is the best possible outcome.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:31.190
Your answer shows only that you're
looking away from the nature of the problem.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:34.490
It's the foolish answer of someone
who doesn't understand the premise.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.990
The premise?

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:37.070
Yes.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.830
You can't do the impossible.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:42.750
In the thought experiment of
Carneades' plank, one of them has to die.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:45.250
That's the premise of the problem, an absolute rule.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:47.040
You should be able to understand that much.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.590
I know one similar story.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:55.630
A certain boy had a special ability.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:09:01.810
Anything he touched with his right hand
would stop changing, as if frozen in time.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:06.190
One day, a man appeared before him.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:09.110
A man who protects the rules of the world.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.530
However, if the man died,
the rules of the world would change,

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.450
and humanity would fall into chaos.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.700
To prevent that,

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:21.080
the man had no choice but to have
his time stopped to never die.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:25.620
And so the boy stopped his time,
to protect the rules of the world.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.830
He chose to sacrifice one man

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:30.630
for humanity to live in happiness.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:33.050
And here's the problem.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:36.090
Did he make the right choice?

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.690
So what is it?

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:50.060
He stopped the time of one man
for the good of the world.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.900
Do you think he made the right choice?

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:56.150
That's a cruel joke.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.570
What Kagaya did was right,

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:01.160
and he didn't have a choice to begin with.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:04.120
The Bureau enforced it.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:08.000
Then let's imagine Kagaya's guilt prevented
him from stopping your father's time

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.000
and that he opposed the Bureau's decision.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.920
Would you think of that as evil?

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:20.510
If killing a person for the absolute happiness
of everyone else is too difficult,

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:23.100
if making the decision to sacrifice
someone is too much,

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.520
would you call that evil?

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.100
Yes, it is evil.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.350
Because it's not the right decision.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:31.190
If you're giving up to your weakness or kindness,

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.440
that's foolish and harmful to society.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.900
Your beliefs are strong.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.700
Strong and righteous.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:38.700
But, Urachi,

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:42.910
can you ask of all humanity to be as strong as you?

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:45.370
You're very strong.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.450
Now you need to learn how it is to be weak.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:52.080
Honestly, I don't think there are
wrong answers to a problem like that.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:55.210
You should choose whatever
you yourself find acceptable.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.760
My answer is to save both.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:04.720
You said it's the foolish answer of someone who
doesn't understand the premise of the problem.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.470
I'm sure you're right.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:11.770
But if you thought about it more realistically,
you'd focus more on something completely different.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:13.520
What you really should consider

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.820
is how to prevent such an accident
from happening ever again.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:20.740
And in case it does happen again,

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:24.030
you should be prepared so that
you can save both of them.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:26.120
Asai,

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:28.040
what are you even talking about?

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:32.500
About the abilities in Sakurada, of course.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:36.920
I'm saying we should think how to
save everyone in the upcoming future.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.510
Who is everyone?

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:41.090
Kagaya, your parents,

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:43.180
and you as well.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.550
I'm happy even now.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.720
If abilities disappear, all the more.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.770
What about the other three?

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:54.400
What can be done to make Kagaya
stop feeling guilty towards you?

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:58.690
Release my parents from the ability binding them.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:11:59.780
Exactly.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.200
That's obviously impossible!

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:06.080
My father's ability must be
protected no matter what.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:09.450
Without it, the world would be thrown into chaos.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:10.700
That's true.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.750
But what matters is his ability, not him.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:17.800
We just need to take the ability from your father.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:19.550
Urachi,

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:23.760
you should just have Sakagami
copy the ability of your father.

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:27.810
Once it's transferred onto another person,
Kagaya would then lock that person,

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:30.100
and your father would be free.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:32.020
That changes nothing.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:35.690
It just means someone else would have
to be sacrificed instead of my father.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.900
What if it's not human?

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:39.610
For example,

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:43.400
what if we try to copy the ability onto a cat?

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:44.990
A cat?

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:49.080
We'd sacrifice a cat instead of a human.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:52.080
Both Kagaya and your father would be saved.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:54.080
That's impossible.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:58.170
There have been no cases of anything
other than human using an ability so far.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:01.010
Also, Sakagami Yousuke's ability...

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:04.380
Like I thought, he can copy only to humans.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:07.970
Why do you think it's not possible
to copy to anything other than humans?

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.470
Because they have will.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:13.350
Sakurada's abilities don't activate
unless you wish for them to.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:16.190
Cats don't possess the will to use an ability.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:20.900
I have a friend who has an ability
to share her senses with a cat.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:24.650
With it, we can give a cat the
same will a human possesses.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.370
So what?

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:35.040
Even if you assume nothing goes wrong,

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.920
and both my parents and Kagaya
get a happy ending,

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.920
what will that prove?

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.710
You can't say anything about abilities

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:45.880
just because they saved someone once!

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.340
Cherry-picking examples
where everything went right

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.220
is no reason to approve of abilities!

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:51.220
Then...

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:55.770
How many people would have to be saved
for abilities to be allowed to exist?

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.480
Saving how many people would prove their worth?

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.360
It's not the problem of a simple number.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.480
People can't rely on such
an unreliable thing as abilities!

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:06.110
You have to accept all the despair and trouble

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.740
and live without turning
your eyes away from reality!

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.750
You're the one turning your eyes away from reality.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.620
Abilities are part of our reality,

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:21.250
yet you force them out of your life,
pretending they aren't there.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:24.840
You're the one trying to run away
and shut yourself in your own world!

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:29.720
Asai,

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:34.560
who knows, maybe what
you're saying really is right.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:39.100
But no matter how right you are,
my heart won't budge.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:43.020
I still consider abilities to be evil.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.440
It's an undeniable fact I can't do anything about.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:48.530
It's just as I thought...

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.700
I cannot convince you.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.660
Yes, I knew that.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.790
I'm sorry, Urachi.

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:59.960
I actually wasn't trying to convince you.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:02.960
Thank you, Tomoki.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:03.840
Hm?

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:05.710
Are you done?

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:06.760
Almost.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:09.680
Listen, Kagaya.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:16.430
There's people who can be saved
with abilities, and can't without.

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:23.440
Kei figured you're more important
than Urachi Masamune.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:26.440
You have to make a choice.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:31.490
If you can save the person you want to save,
it is the right choice to do that.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:36.200
If you can solve an old and still relevant problem,
it is the right choice to do that.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:40.000
Kagaya, what will your decision be?

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.130
Kei always says one thing.

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:46.670
Abilities aren't some special powers.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:51.720
They're part of us humans,
just like our limbs or our words.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.850
No matter how we use them,
the nature of the world doesn't change.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:58.270
We can do what is possible,
and we can't do what is impossible.

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:00.980
The same way a mother pats her child's head,

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:02.850
we use our abilities.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:06.940
Kei said it's nothing more than that.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:14.280
Asai Kei simply wishes for the world
around him to become a better place.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.240
<i>Kei is never wrong.</i>

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.040
<i>Not because he's smart,</i>

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.290
<i>not because he's exceptional,</i>

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:24.210
<i>but because his absolute memory</i>

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:27.540
<i>lets him never lose sight of what he considers right.</i>

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:29.550
<i>That's why he can't be wrong.</i>

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:35.760
Please decide if the outcome he suggests
is one you consider happy or not.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:39.640
It's calling Asai Kei.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:41.810
Urachi Masamune is with him.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:55.820
It's what we decided together.

00:16:56.530 --> 00:17:00.830
You're bringing us pure salvation.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:06.330
We knew from the start you'd be born
and that's what let us live happily.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:11.590
So if you ever feel guilty about this,

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.220
you really shouldn't.

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:14.720
Take pride in what you're doing.

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:18.470
Because you're putting your ability to the right use.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.790
Asai Kei,

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:45.910
I will support you in this matter.

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.290
Thank you very much.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.580
Put Director to the phone.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:52.630
It's me.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:56.800
I see.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.350
I understand.

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:10.900
Asai, did everything go as you planned?

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:11.900
Yeah.

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:14.150
Where did I go wrong?

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:16.400
Was it ignoring Kagaya's feelings?

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.990
Your insensitivity towards his feelings

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:22.160
seemed to me like it extended to your own.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.200
My feelings?

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:23.910
Yes.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:27.120
You trusted Kagaya.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:31.210
I'm sure it was a very strong, subconscious trust.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:35.300
That's why it never occurred
to Kagaya to side with us instead.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:37.720
When did you notice that?

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.930
During a time you don't know about.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.550
While the abilities were gone from this town?

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:43.220
Yes.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:45.970
We erased that with a reset.

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:51.980
During that time, I talked with you.

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:54.780
We had a nice little two hour long chat.

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:59.320
Unaware of abilities, you were an ordinary
man working for the government.

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:01.570
During those two hours,

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:04.660
I got to understand you better
than you can imagine.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.870
You're completely different than me.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:13.790
I would never think of such an inefficient method.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:14.670
Urachi.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:17.420
I want to supervise abilities.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:21.550
I want to join the Bureau, gain a lot of authority,

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:26.220
and rebuild the ability supervising system
itself according to my ideals.

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:31.190
So, Urachi, please lend me a hand.

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:33.310
I need you for that.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.570
What are your ideals?

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.320
I want to fight all kinds of misfortune.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:41.700
If possible, get rid of all of it.

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:44.160
Do you really think...

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:47.950
Do you really believe that such an absurd,
childish dream would come true?

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:49.290
Of course it wouldn't.

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:52.790
Still, I want to right all wrongs one by one.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:57.550
Even if my ideals are eternally distant,
I want to keep moving towards them.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:59.380
Urachi.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:02.300
I think we're very alike after all.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:04.970
What differs about us is only
the beginning and the end.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:09.310
I'm sure we can still understand
each other a little bit better.

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:12.440
Even if not fully, I'm sure we can
understand each other enough.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:14.940
That's why, Urachi,

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:18.860
let's be on the same side, even if only formally.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:23.450
You know, Asai, I hate shaking hands.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.530
There's a lot of other things I hate.

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:28.740
Meetings with too many participants,

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:31.370
childish hopes and dreams beyond reason,

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:32.790
other people's hands...

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:34.420
I hate all of that.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:39.880
And to be honest,
I also hate putting things in my pockets.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.400
<i>I wonder if Kei is free tomorrow.</i>

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.980
<i>Where should I invite him?</i>

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:05.530
<i>We get a day off because of the school festival,
so I guess somewhere where we can relax.</i>

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.500
<i>What is this...</i>

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:27.180
<i>Stop! Stop, please! </i>

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:29.510
<i>Goodbye.</i>

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:38.770
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:42.320
<i>I was wrong from the start.</i>

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:45.280
<i>I'm sorry, Kei.</i>

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:50.200
<i>I don't think it was all really for you.</i>

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.450
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:56.540
Next Episode

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:57.960
I want you to play a game with me.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:59.960
I'm sure I can't save you.

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:00.540
It's stupid, isn't it?!

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:01.590
That's so absurd.
It's stupid, isn't it?!

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:02.920
Weren't you waiting for me to come meet him?

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.210
Give up.
Weren't you waiting for me to come meet him?

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:05.010
It truly is my true happiness.

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:06.880
Hey, give me Asai Kei.
It truly is my true happiness.

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:08.550
Hey, give me Asai Kei.

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:10.050
Thank you.

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:20.440
On such a cold dark sky of grey

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:26.650
Rises the sun, which breathes life into it

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:32.910
A scenery so plain and so mundane

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:42.500
And yet it seems to break my heart, it's so dear to me

00:22:43.380 --> 00:22:46.970
As the time never stops passing by

00:22:46.970 --> 00:22:49.340
You get lost while searching for

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:53.220
Pure like the rays of a morning star

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:56.140
What we all yearn for the most

00:22:56.140 --> 00:22:59.560
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:22:59.690 --> 00:23:02.190
Struggling against all your past mistakes

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:05.230
At last from the answer you found kindness fills your heart

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:08.400
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:12.030
And you find it behind a dark veil of sadness

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:14.530
If I closed my eyes and stopped my thoughts

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.290
If it were so simple to just

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:19.290
Lock your own heart

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:22.420
How lovely life would be

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:27.670
But I believe you have the key

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:34.010
To let my soul be free
